<%- include('../partials/header', { page, title: 'DJXpress Admin | Tips & Extras' }) %>

<section style="padding-top: 40px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="flex-between" style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <h1 style="margin:0;">Tips &amp; Extras</h1>
    </div>
    <p class="small-muted" style="margin-bottom: 24px; max-width: 720px;">
      Fill in whatever you want to use &mdash; anything you leave blank is simply hidden. Nothing here goes live until you save, and you can change it any time.
    </p>

    <% if (saved) { %><div class="alert alert-success" style="max-width:720px;">Saved! Your changes are live.</div><% } %>
    <% if (error) { %><div class="alert alert-error" style="max-width:720px;"><%= error %></div><% } %>

    <div class="card" id="payments" style="max-width:720px; margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">&#128179; Online Payments (Stripe)</h3>
      <p class="small-muted">Lets guests buy a small <strong>Photo Pass</strong> on the live page (and, optionally, lets the host pay once for the whole party on their planning page). The moment someone pays it unlocks automatically &mdash; no checking, no button to press. Clients can pay by card, Apple Pay / Google Pay, or <strong>Cash App Pay</strong> (if you switch it on in Stripe).</p>

      <% if (stripeStatus.configured) { %>
        <div class="alert alert-success">&#9989; Stripe is connected in <strong><%= stripeStatus.mode === 'test' ? 'TEST mode (no real money moves)' : 'LIVE mode (real payments)' %></strong>.</div>
      <% } else { %>
        <div class="alert alert-info">&#9888;&#65039; Stripe isn't connected yet. Follow the 5 steps below &mdash; it takes about 10 minutes.</div>
      <% } %>

      <% if (stripeStatus.testResult === 'ok') { %><div class="alert alert-success">Test passed &mdash; Stripe accepted your key.</div><% } %>
      <% if (stripeStatus.testResult === 'fail') { %><div class="alert alert-error">Stripe rejected the key. Double-check you pasted the whole secret key (starts with sk_live_ or sk_test_) with no spaces.</div><% } %>
      <% if (stripeStatus.testResult === 'missing') { %><div class="alert alert-error">No key found yet. Add STRIPE_SECRET_KEY in Render first (step 3).</div><% } %>

      <ul class="small-muted" style="line-height:1.9; padding-left:18px;">
        <li><%- stripeStatus.configured ? '&#9989;' : '&#11036;' %> Secret key added to Render</li>
        <li><%- stripeStatus.webhook ? '&#9989;' : '&#11036;' %> Payment notifications (webhook) connected <span class="small-muted">&mdash; recommended, so payments register even if a client closes the page right after paying</span></li>
        <li><%- stripeStatus.priceOk ? '&#9989;' : '&#11036;' %> A price is set (below)</li>
      </ul>
      <form method="POST" action="/admin/stripe/test" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Test Stripe Connection</button>
      </form>

      <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:700;">Show me the setup steps</summary>
        <ol class="small-muted" style="line-height:1.8; padding-left:20px; margin-top:12px;">
          <li><strong>Make a free Stripe account</strong> at <a href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/register" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dashboard.stripe.com/register</a> and finish "Activate payments" (it asks for your business details and where to send the money &mdash; your bank account).</li>
          <li><strong>Turn on Cash App Pay (optional):</strong> in Stripe go to <em>Settings &rarr; Payment methods</em> and switch on <em>Cash App Pay</em> (and Apple Pay / Google Pay if you like).</li>
          <li><strong>Copy your secret key:</strong> <em>Developers &rarr; API keys &rarr; Secret key &rarr; Reveal</em>. In <a href="https://dashboard.render.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Render</a>, open this site &rarr; <em>Environment</em> &rarr; add a variable named <code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code> and paste the key. (Start with the <em>test</em> key to try it with fake cards; swap in the live key when ready.)</li>
          <li><strong>Connect payment notifications:</strong> in Stripe go to <em>Developers &rarr; Webhooks &rarr; Add endpoint</em>. Endpoint URL: <code><%= stripeStatus.siteUrl %>/api/stripe/webhook</code>. Select these four events: <code>checkout.session.completed</code>, <code>checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded</code>, <code>charge.refunded</code> and <code>charge.dispute.created</code> (the last two switch a pass off if its payment is ever refunded or disputed). Copy the <em>Signing secret</em> (starts with whsec_) and add it in Render as <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Set your price below, save, then press "Test Stripe Connection".</strong> Clients will see the pay button on their planning page. In test mode pay with card number <code>4242 4242 4242 4242</code>, any future date, any CVC.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small-muted">Render restarts the site by itself after you change an environment variable &mdash; wait a minute or two before testing.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <form method="POST" action="/admin/extras" style="max-width:720px;">
      <div class="form-card" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">&#127903;&#65039; Photo Pass Price (per guest)</h3>
        <p class="small-muted">What a single guest pays <strong>once</strong> to unlock photo uploading &mdash; for that person, forever, at every event. They get a short code (like <code>PASS-AB12CD</code>) that their phone remembers; if they switch phones they type the code in. Keep it small &mdash; <strong>$5</strong> is a good number. Stripe keeps about 14.5&cent; + 30&cent; of each one, so you net around $4.55 of a $5 pass. Needs Stripe connected above.</p>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="photopass_price">Photo Pass price (USD)</label>
          <input type="text" id="photopass_price" name="photopass_price" maxlength="12" inputmode="decimal" value="<%= values.photopassPrice %>" placeholder="5" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">&#128248; Host-Pays Photo Wall Price (optional)</h3>
        <p class="small-muted">Optional: let the person who booked you pay <strong>once for the whole party</strong> so all their guests upload for free. They pay on their planning page. Leave blank if you only want guest Photo Passes.</p>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="photowall_price">Price for the whole party (USD)</label>
          <input type="text" id="photowall_price" name="photowall_price" maxlength="12" inputmode="decimal" value="<%= values.photowallPrice %>" placeholder="e.g. 40" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">&#128184; Tip Jar</h3>
        <p class="small-muted">Guests see these as tap-to-pay buttons on the live page, and a scan-to-tip QR code shows on the Big Screen. Tipping is never required &mdash; this just makes it easy. <% if (!features.tips) { %><strong>The Tip Jar is currently switched OFF on the dashboard.</strong><% } %></p>
        <div class="form-grid">
          <div class="field">
            <label for="venmo">Venmo username</label>
            <input type="text" id="venmo" name="venmo" maxlength="60" value="<%= values.venmo %>" placeholder="e.g. DJXpress (no @ needed)" />
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label for="cashapp">Cash App $cashtag</label>
            <input type="text" id="cashapp" name="cashapp" maxlength="60" value="<%= values.cashapp %>" placeholder="e.g. DJXpress (no $ needed)" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="zelle">Zelle (email or phone number)</label>
          <input type="text" id="zelle" name="zelle" maxlength="80" value="<%= values.zelle %>" placeholder="e.g. you@example.com" />
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="tip_message">Message above the buttons</label>
          <input type="text" id="tip_message" name="tip_message" maxlength="140" value="<%= values.tipMessage %>" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">&#127873; Referral Offer</h3>
        <p class="small-muted">Every shared recap page has its own referral code. Friends who book through it show up in your Booking Inquiries marked with which event referred them. Type the perk you want to offer &mdash; leave it blank to just show the code.</p>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="referral_offer">Offer text</label>
          <input type="text" id="referral_offer" name="referral_offer" maxlength="140" value="<%= values.referralOffer %>" placeholder="e.g. $50 off your booking for you and your friend" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card" style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <h3 style="margin-top:0;">&#11088; Google Review Link</h3>
        <p class="small-muted">When a guest leaves a 4 or 5 star review on a recap page, we'll offer them a button to post it on Google too. Paste your Google review link here (in Google Maps, open your business &rarr; <em>Share</em> &rarr; <em>Ask for reviews</em>). Optional.</p>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="google_review_url">Google review link</label>
          <input type="url" id="google_review_url" name="google_review_url" maxlength="300" value="<%= values.googleReviewUrl %>" placeholder="https://g.page/r/..." />
        </div>
      </div>

      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-block">Save Changes</button>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
